# 📊 Retail Sales Exploratory Data Analysis using Python

## 📌 Project Overview

This project performs an Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) of retail sales data using Python.

The analysis focuses on understanding sales and profit performance across customers, cities, product categories, products, orders, and months.

The project transforms raw retail sales data into meaningful business insights using Python-based data analysis and visualization techniques.

---

## 🎯 Business Objective

The objective of this project is to analyze retail sales data and identify important patterns in sales, profit, customer behavior, product performance, category performance, city performance, and monthly trends.

The analysis helps identify top-performing and underperforming areas and provides insights that can support data-driven business decisions.

---

## 📂 Dataset Overview

The dataset contains **20 retail order records** covering the period from **January 2025 to August 2025**.

### Dataset Columns

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| Order_ID | Unique identifier for each order |
| Customer | Customer name |
| City | City where the order was placed |
| Category | Product category |
| Product | Product purchased |
| Quantity | Number of units ordered |
| Sales | Sales value of the order |
| Profit | Profit generated from the order |
| Order_Date | Date of the order |

---

